SUMMARY:Dormition panigiria of Serifos (Ramos\, Skopoi\, Pyrgos\, Liomantra)
LOCATION:Ramos / Pyrgos\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Serifos spreads Dekapentavgoustos over several nights: on the eve (14 Aug) the Panagia chapels at Ramos and Skopoi (Skopiani) and the Evangelistria in Kato Chora celebrate\, on the 15th–16th the feast moves to Pyrgos and Panagia at Liomantra (Sklavogianni)\, and the nine-day (Enniamera) feasts at Kamaroti\, Maskailia and Pente Pigadia run on 20–23 August. Local sources also refer to a three-day 'Xylopanagia' feast at the village of Panagia\; treat that as the 15–16 August cluster. Each is a ktitores' table of fava\, goat and wine with dancing — pick one per night and ask in Livadi which has music.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#ramos-pyrgos-dormition-panigiria-of-serifos-ramos-skopoi-pyr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#ramos-pyrgos-dormition-panigiria-of-serifos-ramos-skopoi-pyr
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
